(My Database Theory) Tj T*
(=================) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1 Difference Between Data and Information) Tj T*
(==========================================) Tj T*
(Data refers to raw, unprocessed facts, figures, or symbols that on their own) Tj T*
(have little or no meaning. For example, the number "42" is a piece of data.) Tj T*
(Information, on the other hand, is data that has been processed, organised, and) Tj T*
(given context to provide meaning. If we know that "42" represents the age of a) Tj T*
(person named John, it becomes information. In essence, data is the input and) Tj T*
(information is the meaningful output produced after processing that data.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2 What is Metadata?) Tj T*
(====================) Tj T*
(Metadata is data that describes other data. It provides context and structure) Tj T*
(that makes raw data easier to understand and interpret. For example, if a) Tj T*
(database stores temperature readings \(17, 25, 20, 24...\), the metadata would) Tj T*
(include information such as the unit of measurement \(Celsius\), the time period) Tj T*
(the readings were taken, and the location. Metadata is essential for extracting) Tj T*
(meaning from data and is a simple but critical form of data processing.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3 What is a DBMS and What Are Its Advantages?) Tj T*
(===============================================) Tj T*
(A Database Management System \(DBMS\) is a collection of programs that manages) Tj T*
(the database structure and controls access to the data stored in the database.) Tj T*
(It acts as an intermediary between the user and the database, receiving) Tj T*
(application requests and translating them into the complex operations needed to) Tj T*
(fulfil those requests.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Advantages of a DBMS:) Tj T*
(- Better data access and security: The DBMS manages database access while) Tj T*
(  enforcing data privacy and security policies, giving users efficient access) Tj T*
(  to data.) Tj T*
(- Improved data integration: It facilitates multiple end-users accessing data) Tj T*
(  in a well-managed manner, providing a clearer and more integrated view of an) Tj T*
(  organisation's operations.) Tj T*
(- Smooth data manipulation: It enables quick answers to on-the-spot requests) Tj T*
(  for reading or updating data.) Tj T*
(- High-quality information: It supports quicker and more informed) Tj T*
(  decision-making, increasing end-user productivit.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Operational vs Analytical Databases) Tj T*
(=======================================) Tj T*
(Operational Databases \(OLTP  Online Transaction Processing\):) Tj T*
(These are designed to support the day-to-day operations of an organisation.) Tj T*
(They store and manage current, detailed data and are optimised for speed and) Tj T*
(efficiency in handling frequent updates and retrievals.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
